      "id": 1,
      "text": "Vilonia was originally called Cypress Township, but settlers renamed it Vilsonia, meaning 'land of two valleys'.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vilonia%2C_Arkansas"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1861, pioneers from North Carolina, Mississippi, and Tennessee settled near Cypress Creek forks in what is now Vilonia.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.cityofvilonia.net/history"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A local lodge operated for nearly seventy years before disbanding, reflecting early community organization.",
